  return (
    <ErrorBoundary
      logger={(error, info) => {
        // sendToMonitoringService({
        //   message: error.message,
        //   stack: error.stack,
        //   componentStack: info.componentStack,
        // });
      }}
    >
      <MainContent />
    </ErrorBoundary>
  );
}
```

The retry button clears the boundary’s error state and attempts to render its children again. If the underlying problem remains, the boundary will catch the error again. Error boundaries catch errors during descendant rendering, constructors, and lifecycle methods, but not event-handler, asynchronous, server-rendering, or boundary-own errors.

