  return (
    <ErrorBoundary
      onError={(error, info) => {
        // sendToLoggingService({ error, componentStack: info.componentStack });
      }}
      onRetry={() => {
        // Optionally reset application state or refetch data.
      }}
    >
      <MyApplication />
    </ErrorBoundary>
  );
}
```

Error boundaries catch errors during rendering, lifecycle methods, and constructors in descendant components. They do not catch errors from event handlers, asynchronous callbacks, server-side rendering, or errors thrown inside the boundary itself.

