Object prop likely gets new reference each parent render. React compares props by reference, not deep value; `{...}` or object literal is always new. Even `React.memo` sees changed prop.

```jsx
const options = useMemo(
  () => ({ color, size }),
  [color, size]
);

return <Child options={options} />;
```

Then memoize child if needed:

```jsx
const Child = React.memo(function Child({ options }) {
  // ...
