PostgreSQL locks matching row during update. Concurrent calls serialize; each receives different incremented value.

If counter row may not exist, use atomic upsert:

```js
const { rows } = await pool.query(
  `INSERT INTO counters (id, value)
   VALUES ($1, 1)
   ON CONFLICT (id)
   DO UPDATE SET value = counters.value + 1
   RETURNING value`,
  [id]
);

return rows[0].value;
