For multiple dependent operations, use transaction plus row lock:

```js
const client = await pool.connect();

try {
  await client.query('BEGIN');

  const { rows } = await client.query(
    `SELECT value
     FROM counters
     WHERE id = $1
     FOR UPDATE`,
    [id]
  );

  const next = rows[0].value + 1;

  await client.query(
    `UPDATE counters SET value = $2 WHERE id = $1`,
    [id, next]
  );

  await client.query('COMMIT');
  return next;
} catch (error) {
  await client.query('ROLLBACK');
  throw error;
} finally {
  client.release();
}
```

Prefer atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING` when increment is only operation. Do not use process-local mutex; it fails across multiple Node.js processes or servers.

